<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#monsoon">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Monsoon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The monsoon is a seasonal reversal of winds that brings heavy summer rains to South and South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>. Monsoon rains governed agriculture and seaborne trade across the region. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer Empire</a> suggest that prolonged droughts and intense monsoon variability may have strained the hydraulic system at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor">Angkor</a> and contributed to its decline.</p></div>
